# =============================================================================
#  CAV.orch - the Connected Autonomous Vehicle (MPAI-CAV V2.0, Connected Autonomous Operation)
#  Workflow Description Language v0.3, AIF V3.0
#
#  One Controller, one Module - the CAV, 1CAV-CAO-V2.0-I01 - which executes continuously: its subsystems
#  (HCI, ESS, AMS, MAS) feed one another, and what one gives another is the Topology's business, never the
#  User Agent's. The User Agent binds a device to every Port of the Module's boundary, each to one Port,
#  by Data Type and Port Number:
#
#    what the vehicle gives the CAV -
#      Camera, Gnss, SpatialData, Weather   what its sensors read
#      BrakeResponse, MotorResponse,
#      WheelResponse                        what its brakes, motor and steering did: the Responses
#                                           of the one device that acts on the world and answers
#      OfflineMap                           the Offline Map, given once
#
#    what the cabin gives the CAV -
#      CabinVoice (OSD-BAO:2)               what the passenger says
#      PointOfView (OSD-OPV)                the point of view the passenger selects to see the environment outside - Position and Orientation -,
#                                           read by the User Agent from the Point of View Acquisition Unit (UNT-POA)
#      AvatarModel                          the avatar the CAV answers with
#
#    what the CAV gives -
#      BrakeCommand, MotorCommand,
#      WheelCommand                         to the vehicle: slow down, move, turn
#      CabinText (OSD-BTO:1)                what the CAV says, in words
#      CabinAvatar (PAF-PAV)                what the CAV says, as its avatar: speech and face
#      UserID                               who the CAV took the passenger to be
#      Recognised (OSD-BTO:2)               what the CAV heard
#      Decision (CAV-AMD)                   the decision of the Autonomous Motion Subsystem on each frame
#
#  The vehicle is a device that acts on the world: when the Module stops or degrades, the User Agent
#  brings it to its safe state - stopped - whatever it was last told (the interlock of the interpreter).
#  The User Agent names no AIM and no subsystem, and depends on nothing of the Module but its boundary.
#  The Controller keeps the Module's Shared Storage where the User decides (Storage).
# =============================================================================

workflow CAV over 1CAV-CAO-V2.0-I01

on Start:

    type    Storage (OSD-BTO-V1.5)
    ask Controller to start
    ask Controller to keep storage in "{Storage}"

    stream  Camera         (OSD-BVO-V1.5:1)  from device "Vehicle"
    stream  Gnss           (CAV-NSO-V2.0)    from device "Vehicle"
    stream  SpatialData    (CAV-SPD-V2.0)    from device "Vehicle"
    stream  Weather        (CAV-WDT-V2.0)    from device "Vehicle"
    stream  BrakeResponse  (CAV-BRR-V2.0)    from device "Vehicle"
    stream  MotorResponse  (CAV-MRP-V2.0)    from device "Vehicle"
    stream  WheelResponse  (CAV-WHR-V2.0)    from device "Vehicle"
    deliver BrakeCommand   (CAV-BRC-V2.0)    to device "Vehicle"
    deliver MotorCommand   (CAV-MRC-V2.0)    to device "Vehicle"
    deliver WheelCommand   (CAV-WHC-V2.0)    to device "Vehicle"

    stream  OfflineMap     (OSD-BOO-V1.5)    from device "Map"

    stream  CabinVoice     (OSD-BAO-V1.5:2)  from device "Cabin"
    stream  PointOfView    (OSD-OPV-V1.5)    from device "PointOfView"
    stream  AvatarModel    (OSD-B3O-V1.5)    from device "Cabin"
    deliver CabinText      (OSD-BTO-V1.5:1)  to device "Cabin"
    deliver CabinAvatar    (PAF-PAV-V1.6)    to device "Cabin"
    deliver UserID         (OSD-IID-V1.5)    to device "Cabin"
    deliver Recognised     (OSD-BTO-V1.5:2)  to device "Hearing"

    deliver Decision       (CAV-AMD-V2.0)    to device "Journal"

    loop until Stop:
        wait 1s

on Stop:
    ask Controller to stop
